AWS_PROJECT_SPECIFICS.md

# AWS CLI installer bundle (local tooling, never commit)
aws/

# Terraform plan files (never commit). A saved plan is a zip carrying a full
# copy of state, so it holds every sensitive value in the clear. The name is
# whatever -out= was given, so these patterns cover the conventional spellings
# rather than one of them: a plan committed under an unmatched name is a
# published secret, and no later rule can unpublish it.
#
# These globs are the convenience, not the control. A name-based rule is exactly
# what failed here once, so the rule that actually holds is
# scripts/ci/check_no_opaque_archives.sh, which refuses any tracked archive by
# its magic bytes wherever it sits and whatever it is called.
tfplan
tfplan.*
*.tfplan
*.plan
plan.out

# Generated cache files (never commit)
legacy_data/legacy_mirror/robots_cache.json

# IFPA membership roster: a normalized extract of the admin membership report
# (names and membership status; no contact data). Operator-provided, not
# regenerable from any committed source, and held locally only as a maintainer
# handoff; never committed (same model as the mirror above).
legacy_data/membership/inputs/membership_input_normalized.csv

# Freestyle research tree: relocated to the maintainers' private repository.
# On a wired machine this path is a repo-root symlink into the private archive;
# the anchored pattern (no trailing slash) covers the symlink itself, and
# ignoring the path keeps future research output from ever becoming committable
# here again.
/exploration

# Freestyle research working tree: relocated to the maintainers' private
# repository. Dated analysis and reports, never a build input and read by no
# script. On a wired machine this path is a symlink into the private archive; the
# anchored pattern covers the symlink itself, and ignoring the path keeps future
# research output from becoming committable here again.
/freestyle/research

# Person-attributed freestyle adjudications worklist: relocated to the
# maintainers' private repository. On a wired machine this path is a symlink to
# the private copy so the pipeline scripts keep reading their default path.
legacy_data/freestyle_reconciliation/james_adjudications.csv

