# Working notes, planning documents, handovers and operator runbooks live in the
# maintainers' private operations checkout and are gitignored there, not here.
# Keeping them out of this checkout entirely means tracker content, production
# hostnames and console steps are never one `git add` away from a public commit.
# Look for them beside the private ops docs; the cross-session tracker issue
# review and the container-hardening runbook are both there.

# An unrelated client website that happens to sit here on this machine. It holds
# another business's private domain, mail and deployment notes, and a personal
# photograph, none of which belong in this repository's history.
/Raych/

# Mutation-testing sandbox. The runner copies the project here to mutate it,
# and needs it beside the project so module resolution still works. Its report
# and incremental cache are written outside the repository entirely.
/.stryker-tmp/
